                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Great little game, with a load of charm, played it lots on switch many years ago. Not just an arcadey game but is kind of like a twin-stick shooter with a bit of rpg and roguelite mixed in. Different wizards have different specialties, and you can have a healer-specialist friend (probably playing Gislan). Coop is a blast, if a bit hectic, but it really adds to the fun.... since there is friendly fire. It adds an aspect of thinking and positioning and spell choices and that classic je ne sais quoi of friendslop shennanigans. If you have one of THOSE friends, you can split it 50/50 to add some hand-slapping to the main player, or even invert it 100%.\r\n\r\nAlso on the friendly-fire chain... enemies can also friendly fire each other, as well as their healing will heal you or your healing can also heal enemies. Which is notable because some healing spells you will put down a heal-circle, and enemies can walk on it, but you can also steal enemy healing or get them to attack each other. But another cool thing is that a healing-spell dedicated player can actually decimate the purple enemies, since death element is damaged by healing. There are many different spells types to pick from with different aspects, so like....   beams spells have a beamclash/beammerge mechanic and are reflected by shields. Sprays/Cones are shorter range but more aoe and pass through shields. And then there are some wacky/different spells like a flower that makes waves on the ground you can dodge by jumping, just a big 4way flamethrower that rotates slowly.   \r\n\r\nYou start with 2 characters unlocked and as you play you can get more characters through miniquests/challenges at specific points in the story, and unlock character archetypes with achievements (such as \"have 3 healing spells\"). Character archetypes change out your starting spells and unlock a new passive tree. Yep theres metaprogression passive trees too! Your chars level up as you play and gain points for these trees, which help cement the characters identity, so Carabel the ice mage could focus more heavy in freezing enemies, or in just being heavily resistant to damage. There's variety in replays between your char+archetype+passives and which spells you pick up through the course of the campaign (beat boss = pick 1 of 3). \r\n\r\nI have played this on steamdeck and steamframe standalone and they work well. Remote play with your friends works great.",
